		<div class="long">
			<div class="head">
									<div class="options">
						<a href="javascript:;" onclick="togglePostFold(event,2576426)" class="btn btn-default btn-small btn-sm">Fold</a>
					</div>
								<div class="title" id="post-title-2576426">
																		
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/scorpion451" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1918720); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1918720&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606056393" alt="Scorpion451" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1918720)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/scorpion451" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1918720); return false;" >Scorpion451</a></span> <span class="odate time_1472225123 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">26 Aug 2016 15:25</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2576426">
									

<p>Suggestions:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;interviews&nbsp;and&nbsp;professional&nbsp;detachment:</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;interviews&nbsp;and&nbsp;professional&nbsp;detachment</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Dr █████:</strong> Hello SCP-####<br />
<strong>SCP-####:</strong> HRRGG!<br />
<em>SCP-#### proceeded to breach containment resulting in the destruction of $45 million dollars of foundation property and the deaths of 2473 agents, 342 staff, and an ice cream vendor who happened to be driving past the site.</em></p>
</blockquote>
<p>Do not: use an interview as an excuse to show how good at killing stuff your monster is.<br />
Do: assume reasonable security measures for interviews, and keep in mind that implied violence is scarier than stated violence.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>(SCP-####-4 is a hair dryer)<br />
<strong>Dr █████:</strong> Hello SCP-####-4<br />
<strong>SCP-####-4:</strong> Hello Dr █████<br />
<strong>Dr █████:</strong> So, given that we are so completely unsurprised by the fact you are sapient and can talk that we didn't even feel it warranted mentioning in your documentation, we'd like to ask a few questions about that building we found you in.<br />
<strong>SCP-####-4:</strong> Gladly! So I had just graduated with my MBA from Stanford&#8230;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Do not: suddenly make your SCP sapient and able to talk just so you can have an interview to conveniently include exposition<br />
Do: at least mention that the thing can talk if you can't figure out a less jarring way to explain what's going on&#8230; and keep in mind that a talking hair dryer is weird by anyone's standards.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Dr █████:</strong> Hello SCP-####<br />
<strong>SCP-####:</strong> As I have mentioned previously, I am very uncomfortable with being called SCP-####, and while I would prefer my chosen name &quot;Ninjacutioner&quot; I will settle for Mike or Mr. Kolbert.<br />
<strong>Dr █████:</strong> I'm afraid I can't do that SCP-####, despite the last two options being entirely reasonable deviations from normal protocol to put you at ease.<br />
<strong>SCP-####:</strong> ENRAGED SCREAMING!<br />
<strong>Dr █████:</strong> Let the record note that SCP-#### is displaying unprovoked aggression. Recommend sedation and additional restraints for future interviews.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Dr █████:</strong> Hey Ninjacutioner, wanna talk about that huge scar over your heart?<br />
<strong>SCP-####:</strong> Not really.<br />
<strong>Dr █████:</strong> Ok. We still on for lunch later? Taco day in the cafeteria.<br />
<strong>SCP-####:</strong> Awesome!</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Do not: portray Foundation interviewers as completely oblivious robots <strong>or</strong> as overly fraternal with anomalous entities.<br />
Do: assume that they attempt to balance professional detachment with reasonable efforts to establish a comfortable rapport with subjects.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

